<body lang=3D"EN-GB" link=3D"#0563C1" vlink=3D"#954F72">
<div class=3D"WordSection1">
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">A couple of comments on draft-ietf-tls-tls13-vectors=
-06:<o:p></o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-a=
lt:auto"><span style=3D"font-size:12.0pt;color:black">Ordering of messages:
<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<ul type=3D"disc">
<li class=3D"MsoListParagraph" style=3D"color:black;mso-margin-top-alt:auto=
;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;margin-left:0cm;mso-list:l1 level1 lfo2">
<span style=3D"font-size:12.0pt">Whenever the steps &#8216;{server} &nbsp;d=
erive secret &quot;tls13 c hs traffic&quot;:&#8217; and &#8216;{server} &nb=
sp;derive secret &quot;tls13 s hs traffic&quot;:&#8217; appear, this is cor=
responding to the steps in the second phase of the key schedule (section 7.=
1 of tls13-28)<o:p></o:p></span></li><li class=3D"MsoListParagraph" style=
=3D"color:black;mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;margin-l=
eft:0cm;mso-list:l1 level1 lfo2">
<span style=3D"font-size:12.0pt">To complete these you need to have the enc=
oded ServerHello message (as seen in &#8216;Derive-Secret(., &quot;c hs tra=
ffic&quot;, ClientHello...ServerHello)&#8217;).<o:p></o:p></span></li><li c=
lass=3D"MsoListParagraph" style=3D"color:black;mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-=
margin-bottom-alt:auto;margin-left:0cm;mso-list:l1 level1 lfo2">
<span style=3D"font-size:12.0pt">The description of the ServerHello message=
 doesn&#8217;t come until several steps later. Someone using the test vecto=
rs to create unit tests would need to look ahead to the ServerHello payload=
 (after &#8216;{server} &nbsp;send handshake record:&#8217;,
 starting with &#8216;payload (90 octets): &nbsp;02 00 00&#8217;) before th=
ey can recreate the steps above.<o:p></o:p></span></li></ul>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-a=
lt:auto"><span style=3D"font-size:12.0pt;color:black">Coalescence of record=
s:
<br>
There are several examples where multiple messages are shown concatenated, =
both in their payload and ciphertext forms, which makes it much harder to t=
est them. Concatenating them (or not) has no effect on the protocol, so it&=
#8217;s not a requirement. It would be
 helpful to split out the messages so that it&#8217;s clearer which bytes b=
elong to which message. The first example of this is after &quot;{server} &=
nbsp;send a EncryptedExtensions handshake message&quot;, &quot;{server} &nb=
sp;send a Certificate handshake message&quot;, &quot;{server} &nbsp;send a =
CertificateVerify
 handshake message&quot;, and &quot;{server} &nbsp;send a Finished handshak=
e message&quot;; starting with &quot;payload (657 octets): &nbsp;08 00 00&q=
uot;.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<ul type=3D"disc">
<li class=3D"MsoListParagraph" style=3D"color:black;mso-margin-top-alt:auto=
;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;margin-left:0cm;mso-list:l2 level1 lfo4">
<span style=3D"font-size:12.0pt">Mark<o:p></o:p></span></li></ul>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>
</div>
